{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "deck-vs-loan-data",
  "title": "Risk deck against the loan data",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "5324e765-db94-4ed0-bc93-fb6e27211537",
      "question": "The Q3 2026 risk committee deck reports a 30-day delinquency rate for each loan product. Do those figures match what the loan and payment tables show at 30 September 2026?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-03T04:20:53.574354Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-03T04:21:03.658197Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Comparison: Q3 2026 Risk Committee Deck vs. Loan/Payment Tables (as of 30 Sep 2026)**\n\n| Product | Deck (p. 3) | Table (credit_risk_report_delinquency) | Active Loans | 30+ Loans | Match? |\n|---------|-------------|----------------------------------------|--------------|-----------|--------|\n| Personal | 3.3% | 3.35% (7/209) | 209 | 7 | Close (deck rounds to 3.3%, table = 3.35%) |\n| Auto | 4.8% | 4.78% (12/251) | 251 | 12 | Yes (4.78% → 4.8%) |\n| Mortgage | 3.0% | 3.01% (4/133) | 133 | 4 | Yes (3.01% → 3.0%) |\n| **All consumer** | **3.9%** | **3.88% (23/593)** | **593** | **23** | **Yes (3.88% → 3.9%)** |\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. **Auto, Mortgage, and All-consumer figures match** when the table’s rates are rounded to one decimal place (the deck’s apparent precision).\n\n2. **Personal loans show a small discrepancy**: the table computes 7 ÷ 209 = **3.35%**, which would round to **3.4%**, but the deck reports **3.3%**. This suggests the deck may have used a slightly different denominator, truncated instead of rounded, or drawn from a snapshot taken at a slightly different time.\n\n3. **Active-loan counts agree** across all three products (Personal 209, Auto 251, Mortgage 133, Total 593), and the 30+ loan counts (7, 12, 4, 23) also align with the deck’s statement that “23 loans are in the 30-day bucket or worse.”\n\n**Conclusion**: The deck’s delinquency rates are broadly consistent with the underlying loan and payment data, with only the personal-loan figure showing a minor rounding or definitional difference. [1][2]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — q3_2026_risk_committee.pptx — evidence `hermes-receipt:b6153cd95f6e9df71d5ae05b5f7ea180374ae321c5827771de74023c7a8a5ed2`\n- [2] Structured retrieval result — financial_services_banking — evidence `hermes-receipt:398d48f059d76f950a09a81d0e47c52fa95733b1c7bc1488df65dcc4a29b8734`",
