                "title": "q3_2026_risk_committee.pptx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Delinquency: loans 30 or more days past due\nPersonal loans, 30 Sep 2025 = 3.0%. Personal loans, 30 Jun 2026 = 5.9%. Personal loans, 30 Sep 2026 = 3.3%. Personal loans, Change since 30 Jun = -2.6 pts. Auto loans, 30 Sep 2025 = 1.4%. Auto loans, 30 Jun 2026 = 3.1%. Auto loans, 30 Sep 2026 = 4.8%. Auto loans, Change since 30 Jun = +1.7 pts. Mortgages, 30 Sep 2025 = 0.8%. Mortgages, 30 Jun 2026 = 1.5%. Mortgages, 30 Sep 2026 = 3.0%. Mortgages, Change since 30 Jun = +1.5 pts. All consumer loans, 30 Sep 2025 = 1.7%. All consumer loans, 30 Jun 2026 = 3.6%. All consumer loans, 30 Sep 2026 = 3.9%. All consumer loans, Change since 30 Jun = +0.2 pts\n30+ days past due, 30 Sep 2026\nPersonal loans\n3.3%\nAuto loans\n4.8%\nMortgages\n3.0%\nAll consumer loans\n- Across all products 3.9% of active loans were 30 or more days past due at 30 September, against 3.6% at 30 June and 1.7% a year earlier.\n- The highest rate is on auto loans at 4.8%; the lowest is on mortgages at 3.0%.\n- 23 loans are in the 30-day bucket or worse.\n3.9%\nHarborview Community Bank  |  Credit Risk Committee, Q3 2026  |  Synthetic data for a software demonstration\n3",
