                "title": "q3_2026_risk_committee.pptx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Decisions and next steps\n- Note that 30-day delinquency is 3.9%, up from 1.7% a year earlier, and keep the version 5.1 maximum debt-to-income limits, in force since 1 July 2026, under review.\n- Instruct Loan Servicing to contact every borrower that is 30 to 59 days past due within 5 business days, as Table 4 of the Consumer Credit Policy requires.\n- Ask Credit Risk to bring the first results of the monitoring of recent originations required by section 7 of the policy to the next meeting.\n- Approve the allowance for the quarter as presented.\nHarborview Community Bank  |  Credit Risk Committee, Q3 2026  |  Synthetic data for a software demonstration\n8",
